<title>YUGOSLAVIA: TABLE-Yugoslav June retail sales rise 4.0 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Yugoslav June retail sales rise 4.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV RETAIL SALES	JUNE	    MAY	   JUNE 96</p>
<p> change mth/mth		+ 4.0	  + 6.0	    - 1.0</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	    +24.0	  +18.0	    +97.0</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JAN TO JUNE)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	    +20.0	  +19.0	   +103.0</p>
<p>NOTES -- June retail sales were 16 percent above the average for 1996.</p>
<p>Data are preliminary. Data exclude private sector.</p>
<p>Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
</text>
